-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/f746a4d0-b436-4aea-a035-d489d17af275
-- title:
--   Theorem 6 — gradient dominated functions of degree one
-- statement:
--   Let $F\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ be a closed convex set, let $f$ be twice differentiable on $F$ with gradient $f'(x)$ and Hessian $f''(x)$, and let $x_0\in\operatorname{int}F$ be such that the level set $\mathcal L(f(x_0))=\{x: f(x)\le f(x_0)\}$ lies in $\operatorname{int}F$. Assume the Hessian is $L$-Lipschitz on $F$ in the spectral norm, $L>0$ (Assumption 1). Fix $0<L_0\le L$ and let $x_0,x_1,\dots$ be generated by method (3.3): at step $k$ a parameter $M_k\in[L_0,2L]$ is chosen, $x_{k+1}=T_{M_k}(x_k)$ is a global minimizer of the cubic model $\langle f'(x_k),y-x_k\rangle+\frac12\langle f''(x_k)(y-x_k),y-x_k\rangle+\frac{M_k}6\|y-x_k\|^3$, and the acceptance test $f(x_{k+1})\le\bar f_{M_k}(x_k)$ holds.
--
--   Assume $f$ is gradient dominated of degree $p=1$ on $F$ with constant $\tau_f>0$ and minimizer $x^*\in F$ (Definition 3), and let
--   $$\hat\omega=\frac{18}{L_0^2}\,\tau_f^3\,(L+L_0)^3 .$$
--   1. If $f(x_0)-f(x^*)\ge\hat\omega$, then the process converges to the region $\mathcal L(\hat\omega)$ superlinearly:
--   $$\ln\Big(\frac1{\hat\omega}(f(x_k)-f(x^*))\Big)\le\Big(\frac23\Big)^k\ln\Big(\frac1{\hat\omega}(f(x_0)-f(x^*))\Big) ,\qquad(4.11)$$
--   and from some index on $f(x_k)-f(x^*)\le\hat\omega$.
--   2. If $f(x_0)-f(x^*)\le\gamma^2\hat\omega$ for some $\gamma>1$, then for every $k\ge0$
--   $$f(x_k)-f(x^*)\le\hat\omega\cdot\frac{\gamma^2\big(2+\frac32\gamma\big)^2}{\big(2+(k+\frac32)\gamma\big)^2} .\qquad(4.12)$$
--   The first phase is short and the second has the rate $O(1/k^2)$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: f twice differentiable on F → gradient g and Hessian H given by HasGradientWithinAt f (g x) F x and HasFDerivWithinAt g (H x) F x at every x ∈ F; reason: derivatives are relative to F, so no smoothness of the ambient extensions outside F is required; the source derivatives imply these, and on int F they are the ordinary derivatives
--   - encoding: iterates x_0, x_1, … and T_{M_k}(x_k) any global minimizer → 0-based sequence x with the published run predicate IsCubicNewtonRun (any global minimizer, acceptance test as f(x_{k+1}) ≤ f(x_k) + model value); reason: the minimum of the model is attained at x_{k+1}, so this is f̄_{M_k}(x_k); same runs
--   - generalization: (4.11) printed without a range of k; the proof (p. 194) derives it 'as far as δ_k ≥ 1' → (4.11) at every k with f(x_k) − f(x*) > 0; reason: (4.13) gives δ_(k+1)^(3/2) ≤ δ_k for every step, so the logarithmic inequality extends to all positive gaps; the superlinear phase interpretation remains the large-gap phase
--   - encoding: ln of a gap that may be 0 → premise f(x_k) − f(x*) > 0 in (4.11); reason: only excludes ln 0 = −∞, where the source inequality holds trivially
--   - reading: 'the process converges to the region L(ω̂)' → there is k₀ with f(x_k) − f(x*) ≤ ω̂ for all k ≥ k₀; reason: the region is the gap level ω̂ named on p. 194
--   - encoding: ω̂ → a variable ω with ω = (18/L₀²)τ³(L + L₀)³; reason: same constant
-- source:
--   Nesterov & Polyak, Cubic regularization of Newton method and its global performance, Math. Program. Ser. A 108 (2006) 177–205, DOI 10.1007/s10107-006-0706-8, p. 193, Theorem 6, (4.11)–(4.12)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CubicNewton_Shared_IsCubicNewtonRun
import Definitions.Def_CubicNewton_Nonconvex_Supplement_IsGradDominated1

namespace CubicNewton.Nonconvex.Supplement

/-- Nesterov–Polyak 2006, Theorem 6, p. 193. Standing assumptions of Section 2, Assumption 1, a
run of method (3.3) with `0 < L₀ ≤ L`, and `f` gradient dominated of degree `p = 1` with
constant `τ` and global minimizer `xs` (Definition 3). Let
`ω̂ = (18/L₀²) τ³ (L + L₀)³`.
1. If `f(x₀) − f(x*) ≥ ω̂`, then (4.11)
   `ln((f(x_k) − f(x*))/ω̂) ≤ (2/3)^k ln((f(x₀) − f(x*))/ω̂)` holds at every `k` with a positive
   gap, and from some index on `f(x_k) − f(x*) ≤ ω̂` (the process reaches `L(ω̂)`).
2. If `f(x₀) − f(x*) ≤ γ² ω̂` for some `γ > 1`, then for every `k ≥ 0`, (4.12)
   `f(x_k) − f(x*) ≤ ω̂ γ² (2 + (3/2)γ)² / (2 + (k + 3/2)γ)²`. -/
theorem theorem_6 {n : ℕ}
    (F : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ)
    (g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (H : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) →L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (L : ℝ)
    (hF_closed : IsClosed F) (hF_convex : Convex ℝ F)
    (hf : ∀ x ∈ F, HasGradientWithinAt f (g x) F x) (hg : ∀ x ∈ F, HasFDerivWithinAt g (H x) F x)
    (hL : 0 < L) (hLip : ∀ x ∈ F, ∀ y ∈ F, ‖H x - H y‖ ≤ L * ‖x - y‖)
    (x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hx₀ : x₀ ∈ interior F)
    (hlevel : {x | f x ≤ f x₀} ⊆ interior F)
    (L₀ : ℝ) (hL₀ : 0 < L₀) (hL₀L : L₀ ≤ L)
    (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (M : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hrun : CubicNewton.Shared.IsCubicNewtonRun f g H L₀ L x₀ x M)
    (τ : ℝ) (xs : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hgd : IsGradDominated1 F f g τ xs)
    (ω : ℝ) (hω : ω = 18 / L₀ ^ 2 * τ ^ 3 * (L + L₀) ^ 3) :
    (ω ≤ f x₀ - f xs →
      (∀ k : ℕ, 0 < f (x k) - f xs →
        Real.log (1 / ω * (f (x k) - f xs)) ≤ (2 / 3 : ℝ) ^ k * Real.log (1 / ω * (f x₀ - f xs))) ∧
      ∃ k₀ : ℕ, ∀ k ≥ k₀, f (x k) - f xs ≤ ω) ∧
    ∀ γ : ℝ, 1 < γ → f x₀ - f xs ≤ γ ^ 2 * ω →
      ∀ k : ℕ, f (x k) - f xs ≤
        ω * (γ ^ 2 * (2 + 3 / 2 * γ) ^ 2 / (2 + ((k : ℝ) + 3 / 2) * γ) ^ 2) := by sorry

end CubicNewton.Nonconvex.Supplement
